   Recovery of CEE Countries, Univ Econ Bratislava,Dept Bank \& Int
   Finance, Bratislava, SLOVAKIA, SEP 10-11, 2014},
Organization = {Univ Econ Bratislava, Fac Natl Econ; Univ Econ Bratislava, Dept Bank \&
   Int Finance},
Abstract = {The paper focuses on analyzing the relationship between liabilities in
   the banking sector, the monetary aggregates and the interest rates.
   Current trends in the banking sector and the orientation of the cashless
   payments in particular are significantly reflected in the development of
   its liabilities. Relationship among monetary aggregates and the
   development of interbank interest rates and base rates that are
   announced by the central banks indicates the possibility of significant
   future problems. The increase of liabilities in the banking sector
   transforms into pressure on senior bank management to seek appropriate
   opportunities for their investments. Suitable data for analysis were
   obtained primarily from the CNB, so this contribution is dedicated to
   the development of the Czech banking sector. There has not been given
   sufficient attention to this topic yet. However, there is not suitable
   literature, data and documents were obtained primarily in the CNB.},
