Abstract = {Banking is essential to modern economies and nearly half of the world's
   people are unbanked and underserved by banks. The high operating costs
   of banks passed on to retail customers are driving them away who
   otherwise should be in the financial system. Without having access to
   the financial system the unbanked and rural poor have little means to
   engage in mainstream economic activities. A mobile phone-based banking
   system was designed to provide retail banking services to the world's
   unbanked population and rural poor of 2.2 billion based on a cashless
   banking system that reduces operating cost and reduces lending risks and
   therefore can lower the current exorbitant rates charged on retail
   lending and micro-credit. A core-banking server on a low-cost mobile
   device (an Android tablet) could serve over 15,000 micro-banking
   customers. The system definitely appears to be suitable for most retail
   banks or microfinance institutions.},
